#N canvas 30 30 660 640 12;
#X obj 20 15 convolution~;
#X text 130 15 - convolve a signal with an impulse response;
#X text 20 45 Convolves its input with an impulse response held in an
array \, using a partitioned FFT so that a long response costs little
more than a short one. There is no latency: a sample reaches the outlet
in the block that took it in.;
#X text 20 110 Creation: the array holding the impulse response \, and
optionally the tail block size (a power of two \, 4096 by default).
The tail block trades memory and the work done in one call against the
cost of a long response.;
#X obj 20 190 cnv 3 600 3 empty empty empty 8 12 0 14 -228856 -66577 0;
#X text 20 205 Messages;
#X text 30 230 set <array>;
#X text 200 230 read the impulse response again \, from that array or
from the one already named;
#X text 30 275 clear;
#X text 200 275 drop the tail still ringing and start the response again;
#X obj 20 320 cnv 3 600 3 empty empty empty 8 12 0 14 -228856 -66577 0;
#X text 20 335 An array is not watched \, so send set after writing
one.;
#N canvas 40 40 560 460 example 0;
#X obj 20 20 loadbang;
#X msg 20 55 \; ir 0 1;
#X text 90 55 one sample at 1.0: the identity;
#X obj 20 110 osc~ 220;
#X obj 20 145 convolution~ ir;
#X obj 20 180 output~;
#X obj 320 110 table ir 4096;
#X msg 320 60 set ir;
#X text 20 240 Fill the array with a recorded space and the oscillator
is heard in it. soundfiler reads a file into an array.;
#X connect 0 0 1 0;
#X connect 3 0 4 0;
#X connect 4 0 5 0;
#X connect 7 0 4 0;
#X restore 20 380 pd example;
#X text 20 420 See also: soundfiler \, tabread~;
#X text 20 470 pd-convolution is zlib licensed. The convolution is
FFTConvolver by HiFi-LoFi \, which is MIT.;
